GOVERNMENT OF INDIA
MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS
LOK SABHA
UNSTARRED QUESTION NO-1138
ANSWERED ON- 08/12/2023
SUCCESSFUL HOSTING OF G-20 SUMMIT
1138. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH VERMA
SHRIMATI PRATIMA MONDAL
PROF. SOUGATA RAY
Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state :-
(a)  the  key outcomes of the  G-20 Summit  held in New  Delhi  that  have  contributed  to
elevating India’s stature on the global stage along with its likely positive impact on India’s
bid for UNSC membership;
(b) the specific areas of global governance where India’s leadership and initiatives during the
G-20 Summit have been particularly impactful;
(c)  the  steps  taken  by  the  Ministry  to  leverage  the  outcomes  of  the  G-20  Summit  for
strengthening India’s bilateral and multilateral relationships;
(d) the initiatives or agreements, if any, that were introduced during the G-20 Summit, which
have significantly enhanced India’s role in global economic and diplomatic arenas;
(e) the measures implemented by the Government to sustain and build upon the momentum
gained from the successful hosting of the G-20 Summit; and
(f) whether the G-20 meeting has launched any initiative to dilute tension between India and
China and if so, the details thereof?
ANSWER
THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS
(SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)
(a)  The  New  Delhi  G20  Leaders’  Summit  held  on  9-10  September  2023  brought  the
deliberations under India’s G20 Presidency to a successful culmination. Given that G20
comprises of world’s leading economies, accounting for around 85% of the global GDP, 75%
of world trade and 2/3 rdof world population, the New Delhi G20 Summit was a historic
gathering of world leaders. 
The New Delhi G20 Leaders’ Declaration (NDLD) was adopted unanimously by all G20
members on 9 September 2023. It sets out the way forward on a wide range of prevailing
global challenges, including in the following areas:
i. Strong, sustainable, balanced and inclusive growth;
ii. Accelerating progress on Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs);
