(c) G20 outcomes are being pursued and taken forward in our various, relevant bilateral and
multilateral engagements, with a view to further strengthening and deepening our relations
with partner countries.
(d) Some of the new initiatives taken during India’s G20 Presidency were as follows:
i. Disaster Risk Reduction Working Group;
ii. Startup20 Engagement Group;
iii. Chief Scientific Advisors Roundtable; 
iv. G20 Conference on Crime and Security in the Age of NFTs, AI and Metaverse;
v. Session on traditional medicine at the G20 Health Ministerial Meeting;
vi. Agreement on establishing a Working Group on Empowerment of Women; and 
vii. Agreement to strengthen cooperation in counter narcotics.
(e) It is Government of India’s constant endeavour to promote and further build upon the
achievements of the New Delhi G20 Summit, on logistics as well as substance. A virtual G20
Leaders’ Summit  was  held  on  22  November  2023,  to  review  the  agreed  outcomes  and
accelerate progress on them. The themes and achievements of India’s G20 Presidency will
continue to remain an integral part of India’s policy priorities, nationally as well as on the
international  stage.  These  would  include,  inter-alia,  a  human-centric  approach  to
development, food and health security, reform of global governance structures, climate and
environmental  action,  transparent  management  of  debt,  women-led  development,  skilled
migration, and promotion of SMEs – under our overall vision of One Earth, One Family, One
Future.
(f)  G20  is  the  premier  multilateral  forum  for  international  economic  cooperation  and
deliberations on global economic challenges.
